            0.828,
            0.239
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "7. Will the cell having the largest number in a table always be a supercell? Can the cell having the smallest number in a table be a supercell? Why or why not?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 4,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.245,
            0.828,
            0.289
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "8. Fill a table such that the cell having the second largest number is not a supercell."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 5,
          "bbox": [
            0.197,
            0.296,
            0.829,
            0.363
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "9. Fill a table such that the cell having the second largest number is not a supercell but the second smallest number is a supercell. Is it possible?"
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 6,
          "bbox": [
            0.198,
            0.37,
            0.827,
            0.413
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "10. Make other variations of this puzzle and challenge your classmates."
            }
          ]
        },
        {
          "type": "text",
          "index": 7,
          "bbox": [
            0.164,
            0.421,
            0.669,
            0.442
          ],
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "text",
              "content": "Let’s do the supercells activity with more rows."
